I left out the `http-client` enrichment fetch, so the world imports only `state-rw`. I didn't re-add the part of my earlier response that the classifier stopped.

The node records each considered id as seen in the `seen` store. It writes nothing when the digest wasn't published, so those items are picked up again on the next run. The output is `RunReport { date, recorded }`, where `recorded` counts only the ids newly written.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if state_rw::get(id).is_none() {
                    state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                    recorded += 1;
                }
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

